{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["לשלח אותו לעזאזל המדברה — by its plain sense: to send it alive to the mountains that are in the wilderness, as we find in the bird of the metzora: ״ושלח את הצפור החיה על פני השדה״ — to purify him of his impurity; so too here, to purify Israel of their sins, he sends it to the wilderness, which is a place of grazing for animals, as written: ״וינהג את הצאן אחר המדבר״. And in the Talmud: מדבריות ביתיות, in tractate Betzah." "לעזאזל — the lamed is extra in the word למ״ד, like בית ארבאל, which is from the root וארב לו. And likewise the mem of ריקם and חנם is extra for formatting the form of the word, like the nun of שגעון and עצבון and עשרון. [ולפנינו קורא המקום שמשתלח שם השעיר ארץ] גזרה — a desolate land in which there is no produce at all, for it is cut off and severed from all good."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The bracketed clause [ולפנינו קורא המקום שמשתלח שם השעיר ארץ] is textually uncertain and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally. 'Formatting the form of the word' renders לתיקון פעולה, Rashbam's grammatical term for an added letter that shapes the word's structure."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:58.906771710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}